WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.277 --> 00:00:03.314
- Carson is the dog, and I am
the cat in our relationship.

00:00:03.314 --> 00:00:05.524
He's like, love me, love
me, love me, love me,

00:00:05.524 --> 00:00:08.141
and I'm like, oh, I'll think about it.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.474
- Not quite yet.

00:00:11.132 --> 00:00:12.330
We ended up settling upon this place,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.460
and we walked in and immediately,
we saw the tall ceilings.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.702
It had an actual place
we can park outside,

00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:19.400
and I was like, oh my,
take my money please.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.282
But we have, as you can
see, a lot of space to fill.

00:00:22.282 --> 00:00:25.077
- I'm a little bit bohemian when it comes

00:00:25.077 --> 00:00:26.571
to my personal style.

00:00:26.571 --> 00:00:30.739
I know that Carson's not as
bohemian as I am (laughs).

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:33.164
- If we have a huge room,
we're gonna need a big TV.

00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:34.882
- How big a TV do you want?

00:00:34.882 --> 00:00:38.661
- Um, is there really a
size that's big enough?

00:00:38.661 --> 00:00:41.661
(upbeat drum music)

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.069
Search for the couch first, obviously.

00:00:48.069 --> 00:00:49.368
- Yep, modern couch.

00:00:49.368 --> 00:00:50.959
- Modern couch.

00:00:50.959 --> 00:00:52.959
- Look at that one, wow!

00:00:54.102 --> 00:00:56.434
You could seat like 10 people on that.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.060
- That looks really nice.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.251
- Let's make a bid.

00:00:59.251 --> 00:01:01.617
- Let's chat with Nicholas Y.

00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:04.322
- Nicholas, why don't you
want your couch anymore?

00:01:04.322 --> 00:01:05.155
It's beautiful.

00:01:05.155 --> 00:01:07.153
I think he's going to love that message.

00:01:07.153 --> 00:01:09.083
- Standing desk, how about this one?

00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:12.501
- That is cool, I don't
even care where she lives.

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:13.334
I want it.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.241
- Maybe like a floor lamp?

00:01:14.241 --> 00:01:15.482
- [Miranda] Oh, that's cool.

00:01:15.482 --> 00:01:16.315
- I got a bunch of messages.

00:01:16.315 --> 00:01:17.232
- Wilson the cat.

00:01:17.232 --> 00:01:18.065
- We can put an emoji.

00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:19.432
How about the drooling
puppy that says how much?

00:01:19.432 --> 00:01:20.692
- Okay, perfect.

00:01:20.692 --> 00:01:21.752
I think that's everything.

00:01:21.752 --> 00:01:24.361
- We like gotta start to
pick some of this stuff up.

00:01:24.361 --> 00:01:26.532
We're gonna start all
the way up in Studio City

00:01:26.532 --> 00:01:28.222
to get your standing desk, and then

00:01:28.222 --> 00:01:29.533
we're just gonna make a big loop around

00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:31.679
going to West Hollywood, Koreatown,

00:01:31.679 --> 00:01:34.621
Mid-Wilshire, Miracle
Mile, and then finally

00:01:34.621 --> 00:01:36.122
back to Hollywood, and then to our house.

00:01:36.122 --> 00:01:38.677
So, it's a long day, but
we do have one of the vans

00:01:38.677 --> 00:01:40.011
following us, so we can
put all the big things

00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:41.042
in there, make it really easy.

00:01:41.042 --> 00:01:43.744
- And you're driving,
so my job's really easy.

00:01:43.744 --> 00:01:47.041
- It is, you could just sit
here and do nothing, I guess.

00:01:47.041 --> 00:01:48.820
- No, I'll probably keep shopping.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.851
- No, we have so much.
- Just a couple more things.

00:01:50.851 --> 00:01:52.899
- We are so close to
being over our budget.

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:56.321
- I'm gonna look for like one more lamp.

00:01:56.321 --> 00:01:57.979
Let's look at throw pillows.

00:01:57.979 --> 00:02:02.146
I'm just gonna look for plants (laughs).

00:02:03.545 --> 00:02:05.922
(screams happily) It's so cool!

00:02:05.922 --> 00:02:08.589
(upbeat music)

00:02:17.172 --> 00:02:20.255
(uptempo drum music)

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.403
- All right, off to get the couch.

00:02:26.403 --> 00:02:28.583
- Yeah, and then we're close to home.

00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:31.384
- But we may need to run
one little more stop.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.467
- Oh, the TV.

00:02:37.604 --> 00:02:38.499
- It's awesome.

00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:39.954
- It looks just like the real chair.

00:02:39.954 --> 00:02:40.787
Let's see, oh!

00:02:40.787 --> 00:02:41.684
- Do you have ten?

00:02:41.684 --> 00:02:44.222
- Oh, he comes and asks for change.

00:02:44.222 --> 00:02:45.504
Let's see, you're lucky.

00:02:45.504 --> 00:02:47.162
- Hey! (laughs) All right, man.

00:02:47.162 --> 00:02:48.295
- You buy a couch.

00:02:48.295 --> 00:02:49.545
- Hello, couch.

00:02:52.277 --> 00:02:54.854
- We get the rug, and
that leaves literally

00:02:54.854 --> 00:02:57.564
just enough to get your TV.

00:02:57.564 --> 00:02:58.624
- It does?

00:02:58.624 --> 00:02:59.791
- Just enough.

00:03:00.684 --> 00:03:03.543
Oh my gosh, you're so
happy right now (laughs).

00:03:03.543 --> 00:03:04.664
- What are all the letters?

00:03:04.664 --> 00:03:05.747
- Four K, HD,

00:03:06.805 --> 00:03:07.638
two 40 HZ

00:03:09.863 --> 00:03:10.780
- LED, yes!

00:03:11.714 --> 00:03:14.797
(upbeat bongo music)

00:03:21.692 --> 00:03:22.842
- [Couple] We did it!

00:03:22.842 --> 00:03:25.282
- I'm honestly surprised
that we got it done.

00:03:25.282 --> 00:03:28.972
Looking around at this room,
it has so much character.

00:03:28.972 --> 00:03:32.360
Our previous furniture has
all been from big box stores,

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.762
and it is not nearly this charming.

00:03:34.762 --> 00:03:37.072
- Everyone we interacted
with today was so nice.

00:03:37.072 --> 00:03:37.914
- Yeah.

00:03:37.914 --> 00:03:39.370
- And like, take their lightly-used stuff,

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.064
and now it's a part of
our home, and that's just

00:03:41.064 --> 00:03:42.041
kind of awesome.

00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:44.132
- And I'm shocked that
Carson hasn't mentioned this.

00:03:44.132 --> 00:03:45.104
He got his TV.

00:03:45.104 --> 00:03:46.192
- I got the TV!

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:50.109
(upbeat electric guitar music)

